  "text": "For this manager, the fix wasn't another push. It meant explaining what the department needed to achieve, and how each person's work fed into it — then asking each of them for one improvement toward that goal, agreeing on what they could decide, and answering the proposals already sitting on her desk. That gives a team a reason to choose its own work, and the backing to act on it. Another speech about initiative supplies neither. Before you decide someone doesn't care, ask what they're expected to do, how they'd do it, and what's stopping them. Let their answers decide your next move — not your frustration.",
